// March 29, 2024 — CVE-2024-3094 disclosed; packages pulled.
// Exercises: `reverse: true` (scroll-up advances) + animated `scale`
// on the banner + animated `width` AND `height` on a small progress
// indicator + opacity reveals.
//
// Note on the progress bar styling: Chrome's compositor uses sub-
// pixel edge determination when re-rasterising an element whose
// width/height changes continuously, which leaves visible artifacts
// at the painted edge on every scroll tick. Workaround pattern: keep
// a few pixels of transparent border around the visible content
// (here via `border:4px solid transparent` + `background-clip:padding-
// box`) so the sub-pixel edge calculation lands inside the transparent
// border zone, invisibly, rather than at the visible-fill edge.
{
  title: "Disclosure",
  scroll_range: 1000,
  reverse: true,
  snap_positions: [0, 500, 1000],
  elements: [
    {
      name: "headline",
      markdown: "## March 29, 2024\n\nCVE-2024-3094 published. Distros pulled the affected packages within hours.",
      position: [50, 15], anchor: [50, 0],
      width: 80, height: "auto",
      text_align: "center",
      color: "#2c4d2c",
    },
    // The CVE banner — animated `scale` (CSS transform, GPU-accelerated,
    // no layout-induced rendering artifacts) + opacity for the reveal.
    // Static width / height keeps the layout stable.
    {
      name: "banner",
      html: "<div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:100%;height:100%;background:#c0392b;color:white;font:bold 1.4em -apple-system,sans-serif;text-align:center;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.2)\">CVE-2024-3094<br/>backdoor in upstream xz/liblzma</div>",
      position: [50, 50], anchor: [50, 50],
      width: 70, height: 22,
      scale: { keyframes: [[0, 0.3], [500, 1.0], [1000, 1.0]] },
      opacity: { keyframes: [[0, 0], [400, 1]] },
    },
    // Status bar carrying the animated `width` + `height` feature.
    // The outer HTML element has the animated dimensions; the inner
    // visible rect is inset 4 px on every side via a transparent
    // border, so the painted edge never coincides with the bounding-
    // box edge that the browser re-layouts on each scroll tick. Stale
    // compositor pixels happen in the transparent border, invisibly.
    {
      name: "progress",
      html: "<div style=\"width:100%;height:100%;background:#7a3a3a;border:4px solid transparent;box-sizing:border-box;background-clip:padding-box\"></div>",
      position: [50, 80], anchor: [50, 50],
      width: { keyframes: [[0, 4], [500, 30], [1000, 60]] },
      height: { keyframes: [[0, 1.5], [500, 2.5], [1000, 3.5]] },
    },
    {
      name: "footnote",
      markdown: "*Scroll **up** to walk the timeline backwards — `reverse: true` flips the scrollbar direction.*",
      position: [50, 90], anchor: [50, 50],
      width: 70, height: "auto",
      text_align: "center",
      color: "#5a6675",
      opacity: { keyframes: [[0, 0.5], [500, 1]] },
    },
  ],
}
